elta": " code"}}, {"t": 818, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "."}}, {"t": 820, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "  \n"}}, {"t": 820, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "[d"}}, {"t": 823, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "ocker"}}, {"t": 823, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": ":"}}, {"t": 823, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "cache"}}, {"t": 823, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "/"}}, {"t": 826, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "opt"}}, {"t": 826, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "imize"}}, {"t": 828, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "]"}}, {"t": 828, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": " ["}}, {"t": 831, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "docker"}}, {"t": 833, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": ":"}}, {"t": 835, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "concept"}}, {"t": 835, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "s"}}, {"t": 837, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "/docker"}}, {"t": 837, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "file"}}, {"t": 837, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "]"}}, {"t": 839, "type": "gate.citations", "data": {"passed": true, "cited": ["docker:cache/optimize", "docker:concepts/dockerfile"], "invented": [], "said_not_in_docs": false}}, {"t": 839, "type": "answer", "data": {"text": "Copy only the dependency files first, run `pip install`, then copy the rest of the source.  \nFor example:\n\n```dockerfile\nCOPY requirements.txt .\nRUN pip install -r requirements.txt\n\nCOPY . .\n```\n\nThis way the `pip install` layer is cached and won\u2019t be re\u2011executed when you change source code.  \n[docker:cache/optimize] [docker:concepts/dockerfile]", "citations": [{"n": 1, "tag": "docker:cache/optimize", "source": "docker", "doc": "cache/optimize.md", "lines": "L41-57", "passages": ["in the current directory\nRUN npm install   # Install dependencies\nRUN npm build     # Run build\n```\n\nThis Dockerfile is rather inefficient. Updating any file causes a reinstall of\nall dependencies every time you build the Docker image even if the dependencies\ndidn't change since last time.\n\nInstead, the `COPY` command can be split in two. First, copy over the package\nmanagement files (in this case, `package.json` and `yarn.lock`). Then, install\nthe dependencies. Finally, copy over the project source code, which is subject\nto frequent change."], "url": "https://github.com/docker/docs/blob/ff96ad1711065cf2e9c3f1d701dad04775834f70/content/manuals/build/cache/optimize.md"}, {"n": 2, "tag": "docker:concepts/dockerfile", "source": "docker", "doc": "concepts/dockerfile.md", "lines": "L177-201", "passages": ["dependency required by the\nPython application.\n\n```dockerfile\nRUN pip install flask==3.0.*\n```\n\nA prerequisite for this instruction is that `pip` is installed into the build\ncontainer. The first `RUN` command installs `pip`, which ensures that we can\nuse the command to install the flask web framework.\n\n### Copying files\n\nThe next instruction uses the\n[`COPY` instruction](/reference/dockerfile.md#copy) to copy the\n`hello.py` file from the local build context into the root directory of our image.\n\n```dockerfile\nCOPY hello.py /\n```\n\nA [build context](./context.md) is the set of files that you can access\nin Dockerfile instructions such as `COPY` and `ADD`.\n\nAfter the `COPY` instruction, the `hello.py` file is added to the filesystem\nof the build container.\n\n### Setting environment variables", "order to ship and deploy this application without Docker Build, you would\nneed to make sure that:\n\n- The required runtime dependencies are installed on the server\n- The Python code gets uploaded to the server's filesystem\n- The server starts your application, using the necessary parameters\n\nThe following Dockerfile creates a container image, which has all the\ndependencies installed and that automatically starts your application.\n\n```dockerfile\n# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1\nFROM ubuntu:22.04\n\n# install app dependencies\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y python3 python3-pip\nRUN pip install flask==3.0.*\n\n# install app\nCOPY hello.py /\n\n# final configuration\nENV FLASK_APP=hello\nEXPOSE 8000\nCMD [\"flask\", \"run\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8000\"]\n```"], "url": "https://github.com/docker/docs/blob/ff96ad1711065cf2e9c3f1d701dad04775834f70/content/manuals/build/concepts/dockerfile.md"}]}}, {"t": 839, "type": "done", "data": {"ms_total": 838.7, "llm_ms": 778.2, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 298, "prompt_tokens": 1179, "total_tokens": 1477, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 203}, "queue_time": 0.243072829, "prompt_time": 0.082238833, "completion_time": 0.343777002, "total_time": 0.426015835}, "ratelimit": {"limit-requests": "1000", "limit-tokens": "8000", "remaining-requests": "987", "remaining-tokens": "698", "reset-requests": "18m43.2s", "reset-tokens": "54.765s"}}}]}